00:25:18.120 --> 00:25:22.120
And you're like, well, Roy just, you know, slammed me to the ground.

480
00:25:22.480 --> 00:25:22.860
Exactly.

481
00:25:23.180 --> 00:25:23.760
Oh, man.

482
00:25:23.860 --> 00:25:25.760
And, you know, we saw that life.

483
00:25:25.940 --> 00:25:29.620
You know, we could all understand what that life was going to be like going forward, that

484
00:25:29.620 --> 00:25:34.180
flat line of a life going forward with Roy, as opposed to being with your best friend

485
00:25:34.180 --> 00:25:36.120
who really gets you.

486
00:25:36.380 --> 00:25:36.700
Yeah.

487
00:25:36.840 --> 00:25:37.760
And wants the best friend.

488
00:25:37.900 --> 00:25:38.580
He sees you.

489
00:25:38.660 --> 00:25:39.980
You were seen by Jim.

490
00:25:40.200 --> 00:25:42.220
I mean, such a fantastic relationship.

491
00:25:42.440 --> 00:25:45.000
I remember that is one thing that Greg talked to me about early on.

492
00:25:45.040 --> 00:25:50.220
He said, you know, you're going to really get into the weeds big time on this very precious

493
00:25:50.220 --> 00:25:51.660
storyline that we have.

494
00:25:51.740 --> 00:25:54.920
And he teased some of the story out to me at that point.

