507
00:26:38.920 --> 00:26:43.120
But if this is what is in your heart, then we're here for you.

508
00:26:43.280 --> 00:26:43.760
Oh, my God.

509
00:26:43.860 --> 00:26:44.340
What a gift.

510
00:26:44.600 --> 00:26:45.420
What a gift.

511
00:26:45.680 --> 00:26:46.280
Such a gift.

512
00:26:46.360 --> 00:26:50.860
Because I talk to a lot of acting students and creative students, and they don't have

513
00:26:50.860 --> 00:26:51.520
that support.

514
00:26:51.820 --> 00:26:53.980
And I know how hard that is.

515
00:26:54.140 --> 00:26:56.140
And Pam didn't have it.

516
00:26:56.200 --> 00:27:00.740
I don't imagine, like, her parents were encouraging her to become an artist either,

517
00:27:00.900 --> 00:27:01.180
you know?

518
00:27:01.380 --> 00:27:03.220
She had a good job at Dunder Mifflin.

519
00:27:03.320 --> 00:27:04.020
Well, I fool with it.

520
00:27:04.180 --> 00:27:04.500
Yeah.

521
00:27:04.760 --> 00:27:05.300
I'm sure.

522
00:27:05.540 --> 00:27:05.920
Exactly.

523
00:27:06.060 --> 00:27:07.660
No, but what that, no, it's wonderful.

524
00:27:07.660 --> 00:27:08.600
I had the same thing.

525
00:27:08.720 --> 00:27:12.820
My parents just said, you know, do it, follow your heart, and the rest will follow.

526
00:27:13.040 --> 00:27:15.040
We can't wait to see where it's all going.

527
00:27:15.460 --> 00:27:17.720
And you know that, what a wonderful thing.

