00:28:13.020 --> 00:28:14.320
I was really Pam on that.

552
00:28:14.420 --> 00:28:15.520
I was like, oh, that's not for me.

553
00:28:15.780 --> 00:28:16.580
That's rich blood.

554
00:28:16.860 --> 00:28:19.500
I said, they only take like four students.

555
00:28:19.620 --> 00:28:21.340
And he said, yeah, you could be one of those four.

556
00:28:21.540 --> 00:28:22.100
Oh, man.

557
00:28:22.100 --> 00:28:24.920
So I applied, and I couldn't believe it.

558
00:28:24.940 --> 00:28:30.060
I got my acceptance letter on April Fool's Day, and I was so sure that my friends had

559
00:28:30.060 --> 00:28:30.840
pranked me.

560
00:28:30.840 --> 00:28:31.020
Had pranked you?

561
00:28:31.240 --> 00:28:34.940
And it was, I always consider that my first big break, you know.

562
00:28:35.120 --> 00:28:36.420
And yeah, so.

563
00:28:36.660 --> 00:28:38.200
But you had someone that believed in you.

564
00:28:38.200 --> 00:28:40.820
I had someone that believed in me and was pushing me.

565
00:28:41.100 --> 00:28:46.560
So yeah, I think we know that Jim is going to continue to push Pam, and who knows where

566
00:28:46.560 --> 00:28:48.180
that all could go.

567
00:28:48.420 --> 00:28:48.680
Yeah.

568
00:28:48.680 --> 00:28:53.520
We captured some really wonderful moments because of that, not just your arc, but everybody

569
00:28:53.520 --> 00:28:55.880
else and kind of where they were and what they were doing.

570
00:28:56.120 --> 00:28:56.300
Yeah.

571
00:28:56.680 --> 00:29:00.040
How checked out they were of the whole process or how committed they were.

572
00:29:00.660 --> 00:29:02.140
Or how judgy they were.

573
00:29:02.280 --> 00:29:03.420
How judgy they were.

574
00:29:05.000 --> 00:29:08.180
Do you ever think how fun it would be to just go back there again?

575
00:29:08.180 --> 00:29:12.000
If they talked to you guys about, wouldn't it be just dreamy to do a reunion show?

